 "text": "Hey there, how are you? Sure. Complementary colors are those that are firmly marked by their contrast. For example, green and yellow together, or pink and blue. In painting, using complementary colors can make your colors look brighter and stronger. That's right. Black is cold and depletes the light, so it' best avoided for shadows. Yellow and red complement each other nicely. You' save money in the long run. Stick with basic colours for a while, and save the fancy stuff for special projects.",
